Evidence-Bound Review 0.1.0

This standalone extraction was prepared from TAgent's own office-report
constraint checks, under the user's instruction to make small reusable
open-source components. Source references within TAgent:

- packages/tagent-core/src/office-grounding.ts
- packages/tagent-core/src/__tests__/office-grounding.test.ts
- packages/tagent-core/src/research-window.ts
- packages/tagent-core/src/research-evidence.ts (publication-date constraints)
- packages/tagent-core/src/office-blocks.ts (exact text provenance concept only)

The standalone implementation introduces its own input contract, exact UTF-16
references, explicit citation bindings, resource bounds, ESM API, declarations
and CLI. It is not a drop-in replacement for TAgent's verifier or its benchmark.

Window semantics are explicit: 30 inclusive calendar days means asOf and the
29 preceding days. TAgent's historical rolling-window helper subtracts 30 days;
this package does not silently inherit that older contract.

No third-party Markdown parser, model SDK, user conversation, credential,
retrieved article, or other private data is bundled. Examples and regression
materials are synthetic. There are no runtime or development dependencies in
package.json, and no network or model calls in tests.

The LICENSE file covers this extracted directory. It does not assert a license
for the rest of the TAgent repository, for external sources supplied by users,
or for any third-party package.

